ype": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Relate information about problems.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect Continuous vs. Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. <br/><br/>You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experiences.<br/>When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. <br> To emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">result of the action</span>, use the simple form.<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Has anyone called the police?</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect Continuous tense </span> to describe:<ul><li> a single activity that lasts a long time </li><li> an action that is repeated over a long period of time</li></ul>These continue up to the present.  You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Continuous tense </span> when a long activity has just stopped. <br> To emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">action</span>, use the continuous form.<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">What have the other people in the cafe been doing?</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> There have been other guests.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" before now there were some\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The geckos have been choosing to sneak in to keep warm on cold nights.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" they've done this for a while now\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Silver dollar sized spiders have greeted me as I open the medicine cabinet in the morning. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Others have been lurking under the toilet seat. I have been gently lifting it with a wooden spoon before I sit since the first sighting. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There have been other guests. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The geckos have been choosing to sneak in to keep warm on cold nights. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There's been a warning in the paper about the venomous cyclopean snake that lurks in the tall grass near the beach at this time of year. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Needless to say I've been sticking to the sand and walkways. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Gerunds and Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by a gerund:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "propose (doing)<br/>keep (doing)<br/>consider (doing)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">appreciate having</span> new experiences.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by an infinitive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "expect (to do)<br/>happen (to do)<br/>choose (to do)<br/>stick (to do)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">expected to</span> find life to be pretty much the same.  </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I have always <span class=\"strong\">considered living</span> in a city best for me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When my firm <span class=\"strong\">proposed sending</span> me to Australia for a while, I jumped at the chance. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They disappear quickly, but \"where to?\", I <span class=\"strong\">keep asking</span> myself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'd <span class=\"strong\">happened to</span> see  one or two in picture books before.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The geckos have been <span class=\"strong\">choosing to</span> sneak in to keep warm.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I've been <span class=\"strong\">sticking to</span> the sand and walkways. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to jump at the chance", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to seize the opportunity to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When my firm proposed sending me to Australia for a while, I jumped at the chance. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about encountering strange new animals.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "miner", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who works in a mine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've met a few of the locals in or near my tiny miner's cottage. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tease", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to irritate or bother", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They have been teasing me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lizard", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a reptile with scales", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A 12 inch black and white lizard was hiding under it. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lurk", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lie in wait or hide", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Other spiders have been lurking under the toilet seat.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gecko", "type": "name"}, {"content": "any of numerous small, mostly nocturnal tropical lizards ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The geckos have been choosing to sneak in to keep warm on cold nights. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shriek", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a loud, sharp, shrill cry", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The neighbors have been teasing me about the shriek I let out ever since.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "venomous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a gland with poison in it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The venomous cyclopean snake lurks in the tall grass near the beach at this time of year. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le05ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue about animals, insects or reptiles.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the Present Perfect tense and the Present Perfect Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use verb plus gerund and verb plus infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my dialogue with a partner and we read it aloud together.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Two people are having a conversation about animals, insects or reptiles they have encountered in your country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about things that have happened, or things that have been happening.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talk about your attitudes toward an action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your dialogue aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}